
                                                   VIEW COMMAND


View data at a particular address.

Below is the syntax :
                            view 	-t {"IHEX"|"ASCII"}  -addr address  -l len  [-n name]

---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES       |    DESCRIPTION
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -t          |    Specifies type IHEX or ASCII. Mandatory switch.
   -addr       |    Address at which data of specified length is viewed. Mandatory switch.
   -l          |    Specifies the length to be viewed. Mandatory switch.
   -n          |    Specifies the name of the command. Optional.
---------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:
	read -in medc18.hex -igCks true	
	view -t IHEX -addr 0x80030010 -l 0x60
	check -t ASCII -addr 0x80030010 -l 0x32 -n "View Data"
	write -out output.hex -lyt 0x10	
